<title>SPAIN: Spain's Montoro sees room, need for key rate cut.</title>
<headline>Spain's Montoro sees room, need for key rate cut.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Economy Secretary Cristobal Montoro said on Wednesday he considers a cut in key money rates both possible and necessary.</p>
<p>&quot;Lower interest rates are still possible and it is necessary for job creation and improved economic activity,&quot; Montoro told reporters after a parliamentary committee meeting.</p>
<p>The Bank of Spain's key money rate, the repo rate, is currently at 7.25 percent. Some economists think the central bank may ease rates this Friday at its regular repo auction.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
